Declare buildifier_prebuilt's toolchain repo reproducible so it can use the repo contents
cache.

https://github.com/keith/buildifier-prebuilt/pull/120 marked the module *extension*
reproducible via `extension_metadata`, which is a different mechanism; the repo rule itself
still returns nothing, so the toolchains repo is refetched on every CI runner.

Not yet raised upstream.

diff --git a/defs.bzl b/defs.bzl
index db41fa7..9da99a0 100644
--- a/defs.bzl
+++ b/defs.bzl
@@ -27,6 +27,12 @@ declare_toolchain(
         )
     repository_ctx.file("BUILD.bazel", content)
 
+    # Bazel <8.3.0 lacks repository_ctx.repo_metadata
+    if not hasattr(repository_ctx, "repo_metadata"):
+        return None
+
+    return repository_ctx.repo_metadata(reproducible = True)
+
 _buildifier_toolchain_setup = repository_rule(
     implementation = _buildifier_toolchain_setup_impl,
     attrs = {
